# Class: obo:OBI_0000367 (light emission function)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:OBI_0000367 "A light emission function is an excitation function to excite a material to a specific excitation state that it emits light."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:OBI_0000367 "light emission function"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:OBI_0000367 obo:OBI_0000374)

# Class: obo:OBI_0000372 (material separation function)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:OBI_0000372 "A material separation function is a function that increases the resolution between two or more material entities. The  to distinction between the entities is usually based on some associated physical quality."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:OBI_0000372 "material separation function"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:OBI_0000372 obo:BFO_0000034)

# Class: obo:OBI_0000374 (excitation function)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:OBI_0000374 "A excitation function is a function  to inject energy by bombarding a material with energetic particles (e.g., photons) thereby imbuing internal material components such as electrons with additional energy.  These internal, 'excited' particles may lead to the rupturing of covalent chemical bonds or may quickly relax back to there unexcited state with an exponential time course thereby locally emitting energy in the form of photons."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:OBI_0000374 "excitation function"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:OBI_0000374 obo:BFO_0000034)

# Class: obo:OBI_0000378 (filter function)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:OBI_0000378 "A filter function is a function to prevent the flow of certain entities based on a quality or qualities of the entity while allowing entities which have different qualities to pass through"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:OBI_0000378 "filter function"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:OBI_0000378 obo:OBI_0000372)

